{{Italics title}}
'''''Garmugia''''', also referred to as '''''gramugia''''',<ref name="Anderson"/> is an [[Italian cuisine|Italian]] [[soup]] originally from the town of [[Lucca]], Tuscany.<ref name="Johns"/><ref name="Elon"/> The soup's use in the cuisine of Lucca dates back to the 17th century.<ref name="Johns"/><ref name="GTI"/> ''Garmugia'' has been described as "a hearty soup"<ref name="Halpern's"/> that is "unknown outside of the province".<ref name="Johns"/>
